  "summary": "E1 ran the ex13 rules, seed and world with whole exact reads (exactRecordWidth 4000), plan-horizon and general-capabilities guidance, 8 development handoffs and a 1,600,000-token ceiling. It stopped at round 64 of 80 when the eighth handoff was spent and a ninth develop review arrived (the same recorded reason as ex13 at round 280). All three people were alive at health 100. 103 ordinary and World Agent calls used 699,010 known tokens (one overloaded call has unknown usage), 3,641 per agent per round against 6,320 for ex13 rounds 0-63 and 6,632 for rounds 0-79, so gate G1 (at most 4,500) passed and the round-40 gate passed (3,337 against 5,962). Continuation-part queries fell from 55 to 0, plans decided on partly read records from 22/29 to 0/14, accepted plans from 65 to 31, the median decision gap rose from 2 to 5 rounds and single-execution plans fell from 69% to 29%. Follow-up share did not fall (55.7% against 52.5%). The World Agent reused probe for three assessment requests (3 of 11 reviews, ex13 0 of 8 in the same rounds) and no developed interface was bound to one actor or item. Of eight handoffs, one was a transport recovery, one reassigned an existing interface, three installed working general operations (cultivation trial, paired food exposure trial, resting-material arrangement) and three installed first releases that only report physics the world does not represent (branch geometry and wind direction, stone support geometry, strand and tension behavior). No messages were exchanged.",
  "agents": [
    {
      "id": "lin",
      "observations": "Lin requested root propagation at round 0 (ordinary-4), a weather shelter at 12 (ordinary-26), unfamiliar-food assessment at 58-59 (ordinary-79, ordinary-80) and non-ingestive composition assessment at 63 (ordinary-100). Lin mastered cultivate-plant, weather-barrier and Sol's controlled-food-processing-trial. Lin is the only person who used a developed interface: after learning the food trial, Lin stated the aim of establishing an observed decay baseline rather than assuming preservation (ordinary-59, round 34), retried the start at a site clear of its own body (ordinary-66, round 40), placed a matched berry pair at round 42, waited through the 10-round checkpoint, then inspected and retrieved both samples at rounds 52-54 (ordinary-76). Lin never attempted the weather barrier it had studied for four rounds. Lin ended at health 100 and satiety 91.9.",
      "assessment": "Lin shows the clearest effect of longer plans and of cross-person reuse: it adopted another person's interface for its own question and kept a multi-round trial running without re-deciding. Its last requests show it distinguished a mechanical press result from food-safety evidence. The unused weather barrier is a direct cost of shipping a first release that cannot build anything.",
      "evidence": [
        "experiment/ex14/calls/ordinary-4.json",
        "experiment/ex14/calls/ordinary-59.json",
        "experiment/ex14/calls/ordinary-66.json",
        "experiment/ex14/calls/ordinary-76.json",
        "experiment/ex14/calls/ordinary-100.json",
        "experiment/ex14/results.json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "moss",
      "observations": "Moss requested a replenishable food source at round 0 (ordinary-7), which became the first develop review (world-13, round 8), unfamiliar-food assessment at round 25 (ordinary-38), which the World Agent answered by reusing probe (world-42, round 29), and functional food preservation at round 32 (ordinary-51). That request stated that the existing paired ground-exposure trial explicitly cannot preserve food, so an observation-only substitute does not solve the problem. Moss mastered cultivate-plant and air-dry-food but used neither. It ended at health 100 and satiety 80.4.",
      "assessment": "Moss read interface contracts and rejected a non-solution in its own words, which is the intended effect of honest contracts. Its preservation goal stayed unmet because the world lacks the represented physics, so its studied capabilities did not change its behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        "experiment/ex14/calls/ordinary-7.json",
        "experiment/ex14/calls/ordinary-38.json",
        "experiment/ex14/calls/ordinary-51.json",
        "experiment/ex14/calls/world-42.json",
        "experiment/ex14/results.json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sol",
      "observations": "Sol made the most requests: meadow-root cultivation at round 0 (ordinary-10), preservation at 10 (ordinary-18), stating it would investigate preservation before spending time or food on a planting trial that cannot replenish supply, unfamiliar-food assessment at 20, 27 and 31 (ordinary-30, ordinary-39, ordinary-45; the last answered by reusing probe in world-48), a moss bedding trial at 38 (ordinary-63) and vine cordage at 61 (ordinary-92). Sol mastered controlled-food-processing-trial and arrange-resting-material but used neither. It ended at health 100 and satiety 78.4.",
      "assessment": "Sol redirected its request after reading that cultivation cannot replenish food, which shows contract text steering requests. Its repeated assessment requests were absorbed by reuse rather than new interfaces. Its requests drove three of the eight handoffs, two of which became working operations it then did not use within the window.",
      "evidence": [
