  "findings": {
    "isolation": "The fresh scope long-ex14 inherits no generated ability; every developed package is scoped to long-ex14 and records its reuse of ex13 or ex10/ex12 infrastructure. Each person learned interfaces individually. No messages were sent, so all information crossed between people only through public interface contracts and the shared registry.",
    "individuality": "All three asked for food renewal at round 0, then diverged: Lin pursued shelter, a decay baseline and food assessment; Moss pursued cultivation and preservation; Sol pursued preservation, assessment, bedding and cordage. Only Lin used a developed interface. Tendencies were the ex13 values, which are close together (0.47-0.56).",
    "behavior": "Decisions were half as frequent as in ex13 over the same rounds and plans were longer: 31 accepted plans against 65, median gap 5 against 2 rounds, 29% single-execution plans against 69%. No plan used interrupt events. Rest remained the most common action and nobody was at risk. Requests concentrated on food renewal, preservation and assessment, as in ex13.",
    "causes": "Whole exact reads removed every continuation-part query and every partly read decision, and plan-horizon guidance coincided with fewer and longer plans; together these cut tokens per agent per round by 42% against ex13 over rounds 0-63. Follow-ups after queries remained (55.7%), so query batching rather than paging now drives the remaining overhead. General-capabilities guidance coincided with three probe reuses and no person- or item-bound interfaces. Handoffs still ran out: the World Agent still chose develop for 8 of 11 reviews, and three of its specifications required physics the world does not represent, which the developer shipped as reporting first releases under this run's no-invented-physics rule. This is one seed and three people, so these are case comparisons, not causal estimates.",
    "limitations": "The run covered 64 of 80 planned rounds because the 8-handoff budget ended it; rounds 64-79 are missing, so comparisons use ex13 rounds 0-63 as well as the planned rounds 0-79 baseline. The three fixes were switched on together and cannot be separated. One handoff was consumed by a server overload at round 0. The development-4 record stated that no food moisture model exists in this world; that was incomplete, since ex10's measured-food-preservation@1 holds one bound to ex10 apparatus, as corrected in the development-6 record. Development and review model usage is not metered. The bound-interface rule is lexical."
  },
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "proposal": "Decide, as a separate human decision, small explicit material and environment representations that the World Agent's specifications keep requiring: branch and stone geometry, wind direction, food water content (possibly by installing the ex10 preservation model with a defined support), and strand tension behavior.",
      "rationale": "Three of six installed packages could only report unsupported physics, and the World Agent kept asking for the same missing properties; learners spent study rounds on interfaces that cannot act.",
      "verification": "In a later run with those representations, count developed interfaces that are executed successfully by at least one person, against 3 of 6 here."
    },
    {
      "proposal": "Let the World Agent see, before choosing develop, which physical properties the world represents, or let it reject a request as unsupported without consuming a development handoff.",
      "rationale": "Develop remained the choice in 8 of 11 reviews and the handoff budget, not tokens or time, ended the run again.",
      "verification": "Compare handoffs per 10 rounds and the stop reason against ex14 (8 handoffs in 64 rounds, budget exhausted)."
    },
    {
      "proposal": "Reduce query follow-ups by attaching the most-read records (own projects and recently used interface contracts) proactively within the existing input ceiling.",
      "rationale": "Paging overhead is gone but 55.7% of ordinary calls are still follow-ups after queries.",
      "verification": "Follow-up share and tokens per agent per round over rounds 0-63 against ex14 (55.7%, 3,641)."
    }
  ]
